Noise IK TLA+ model

Verifies the internal/noise IK state machine in ../ik.go.

What is modeled in ik.tla

  Initiator iWrote, iFailed, iDone with IWrite, IReadOk, IReadFail.
  Responder rRead, rFailed, rDone with RRead, RWriteOk, RWriteFail.
  Key mirror on success: initiator send equals responder recv and reverse.
  Transport nonces start 0, increment on successful encrypt and decrypt
  only, fail closed, Rekey preserves nonce, cap 3 with terminal overflow.
  Adversary drop, duplicate, replay, tamper. Failed is terminal. No
  deadlock via stuttering Done.

What is checked in ik.cfg

  KeyMirror, TerminalFailed, NoDoubleWrite, NonceMonotonic.
  Liveness to both done on a fair schedule without adversary.

How to verify

  tlc -workers 2 -config internal/noise/tla/ik.cfg internal/noise/tla/ik.tla

Expected: Model checking completed. No error has been found, about
140005 generated and 15592 distinct states, depth 24, about 1s.

Go adherence

  go test -race -run TestModel ./internal/noise/...
  go test -race ./internal/noise/...
  go vet ./internal/noise/...

ik_model_test.go maps IWrite, IRead, RRead, RWrite to real calls plus
key mirror by cross decrypt and nonce rules.
Model drift is safe-direction only: write-path pre-checks fail open without poison and never advance state.
Symmetric transport nonces are unmodeled: each direction starts at 0 and increments independently.
Checked properties transfer because code refines the model: every modeled step maps to a real call.
Model drift (safe direction): write-path pre-checks fail open without
poison, and symmetric nonces are unmodeled. Properties transfer because
the Go code refines the model.
